<section class="sec" id="why">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">Why now</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">Why Salesforce, and <span class="serif">why now.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">Salesforce runs sales and service for the world's enterprises, and its ecosystem cannot hire configured-and-certified people fast enough. Like SAP, it rewards platform specialists: learn one deep system and the demand, and the pay, follows you for a career.</p>
<div class="why-stats">
<div class="ws reveal"><b>#1</b><span class="t">CRM platform globally</span><p>The default customer system of enterprises, with an ecosystem hiring in every metro and GCC.</p></div>
<div class="ws reveal"><b>9.3M</b><span class="t">Ecosystem jobs forecast</span><p>IDC-scale projections keep the Salesforce economy among tech's largest employers.</p></div>
<div class="ws reveal"><b>2-path</b><span class="t">Admin and developer</span><p>Non-coders thrive as admins; coders climb the Apex ladder. This course opens both.</p></div>
</div>
<h3 class="reveal" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:800;font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:44px">Why it is a smart move for you</h3>
