<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>Salesforce or SAP: which should I choose? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both are platform careers with deep demand. SAP suits finance and supply-chain minds; Salesforce suits sales, service and cloud-native builders, with a no-code admin entry. A counsellor can map your background to the better fit honestly.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do I need coding for Salesforce? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Not for the admin path, which alone gets first jobs. The developer half teaches Apex assuming no background, and many admins add it in year two for the salary jump. This course gives you both from day one.</div></details>
<details><summary>Which certifications does the course prepare me for? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Salesforce Certified Administrator (ADM-201) and Platform Developer I, the two filters recruiters apply, each with full mock exams. Exams are booked with Salesforce and charged separately.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the starting salary in the Salesforce ecosystem? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Certified admins typically start between Rs 3.5 and 6 lakh. Admin-plus-developer profiles reach Rs 6 to 11 lakh within two to three years, and consultants and architects climb steeply from there.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is Salesforce demand real in Kerala and the Gulf? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Yes. Consulting majors run large Salesforce practices from Indian delivery centres including Technopark ecosystems, and GCC digital programs hire admins and developers continuously.</div></details>
<details><summary>Will I practise on a real Salesforce system? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">On your own developer org from week one: every module ends in configuration or code living in your org, which becomes demo material in interviews.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala and the GCC. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
</div>
